    "captions": {
      "ruin": "ONE reading, per-cell, copied from Result as-is (D-50). A crossing cell reports at its own t*; a non-crossing cell has no t* and reports at t_now. Only ruin.trad varies with the rate, and only on the 12 Low cells with shocks >= 1. The comparable common-rate reading is scripts/measure_4a.py's, not a second column.",
      "breakeven_objective_5": "Objective 5's break-even is the LEFT EDGE OF A PLATEAU, not a point (D-51). P(not running out) counts a discrete event over n_paths, so its difference is a staircase whose zero set has WIDTH -- 0.1616 pp at the archetype, one step being 1/n_paths. bisection closes on the plateau's left edge. These cells read about 0.08 pp below t_now for that reason and NOT because the slab varies. D-22's claim is asserted directly instead: the after-tax difference is exactly 0.0 at t_now.",
      "dollars_objective_4": "Objective 4 is the 10th percentile of the after-tax TERMINAL distribution, and D-38 floors nothing, so it is a signed number that may be deeply negative. That is arithmetic bisection handles, not a broken cell.",
      "dollars_objective_5": "`dollars` ON THE 12 OBJECTIVE-5 CELLS IS NOT IN DOLLARS. outcome() returns the objective's reduction, and objective 5's reduction is P(not running out) -- a fraction in [0, 1], not a terminal value. The field is filled because Section 5 fills it on every crossing cell and because `roth != trad` still means delta was applied; it is captioned because a reader computing $X from this row would be subtracting two probabilities and printing the answer as money. D-23 pins the app's sentence to objective 4, so the app never reads this. The README's four-objective table does, and must name the unit."
    }
  },
